{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>נורא</b> — Let the fear of Elohim be in the earth from the place of the Temple, in the manner of: \"Blessed be YHWH from Zion.\" And the correct interpretation: the Temple on earth corresponds to the Temple in heaven, as: \"and this is the gate of heaven,\" and it is a hidden sod. And because he stated, \"ascribe strength to Elohim,\" in the utterance that they acknowledge that He is the Master of might, he said that the strength is in actual deed, and the mighty powers HaShem will give them to Israel and they will give thanks to HaShem; therefore, blessed be Elohim."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:20.107401198Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}